---
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import Dashboard from '../../assets/portofolio/optik-system-beranda.png';
import Booking from '../../assets/portofolio/optik-system-booking.png';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><BaseHead title="Optik Siliwangi — A project by Adi" description="A closer look at an optical retail web system: multi-branch operations, staff workflows, and public appointment requests." image={Dashboard}/></head><body><Header/><main id="main" class="container">
<section class="case-intro"><a href="/#work" class="back-link"><Icon name="arrow-left" size={15}/> Selected work</a><div class="eyebrow">Portfolio / Web application / 2026</div><h1>Optik Siliwangi<span>.</span></h1><p class="case-subtitle">A clearer view of<br/><span>everyday operations.</span></p><div class="case-meta"><div><span>Project</span><strong>Optical retail system</strong></div><div><span>Focus</span><strong>Operations & appointment workflows</strong></div><div><span>Built with</span><strong>Laravel · PostgreSQL · Astro</strong></div></div></section>
<figure class="case-image"><div class="image-toolbar"><span>OPTIK SILIWANGI</span><span>01 / OPERATIONS OVERVIEW</span></div><Image src={Dashboard} alt="Optik Siliwangi dashboard showing branch and date filters, lens order statuses, and financial summaries" width={1400} loading="eager"/><figcaption>The staff workspace brings operational status and branch context into one view.</figcaption></figure>
<section class="case-section"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="number">01</span> The context</div><h2>Many moving parts.<br/>One connected workflow.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Optical retail brings together customer records, prescriptions, lens orders, payments, inventory, and examination schedules. Each part has its own status, while staff need to understand how the pieces connect.</p><p>Optik Siliwangi brings those workflows into a web application with branch-aware staff access and a separate public frontend for browsing branches and requesting examinations.</p><p class="evidence-note">This case study describes the interfaces and functionality present in the project. Business impact and customer outcomes have not been measured here.</p></div></section>
<section class="case-section"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="number">02</span> The approach</div><h2>Make the important<br/>differences visible.</h2></div><div class="decisions"><div><span>01</span><div><h3>Keep the branch in context.</h3><p>Branch and date filters give operational summaries a clear scope. Supporting labels explain what a total includes and which event date it uses.</p></div></div><div><span>02</span><div><h3>Show where work stands.</h3><p>Separate waiting, ready, delayed, and collected orders so staff can recognize different stages of the lens workflow.</p></div></div><div><span>03</span><div><h3>Connect the request to the follow-up.</h3><p>Public bookings are recorded as requests. Staff review and follow up through WhatsApp, keeping the difference between requested and confirmed explicit.</p></div></div></div></section>
<figure class="case-image booking-image"><div class="image-toolbar"><span>OPTIK SILIWANGI</span><span>02 / BOOKING WORKSPACE</span></div><Image src={Booking} alt="Optik Siliwangi staff booking management screen" width={1400}/><figcaption>The booking workspace supports the staff side of examination requests.</figcaption></figure>
<section class="case-section"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="number">03</span> Under the surface</div><h2>A focused frontend.<br/>A shared source of truth.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Laravel owns the operational rules and public API. The Astro frontend presents branch details and guides visitors through selecting a branch, a date and time, and their contact information.</p><p>Availability is calculated by the backend. The public flow handles field errors, slots that become unavailable, and connection failures. Request identifiers help protect repeated submissions from producing duplicate bookings.</p><div class="stack"><span class="pill">Laravel</span><span class="pill">PostgreSQL</span><span class="pill">Astro</span><span class="pill">Public API</span><span class="pill">Multi-branch workflows</span></div></div></section>
<section class="flow-section"><div class="eyebrow">One workflow, two perspectives</div><div class="flow"><div><span>PUBLIC EXPERIENCE</span><h3>Find a branch.<br/>Request a time.</h3><p>Astro frontend</p></div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↔</span><div><span>SHARED RULES</span><h3>Availability.<br/>Validation. Status.</h3><p>Laravel API</p></div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↔</span><div><span>STAFF WORKSPACE</span><h3>Review requests.<br/>Follow up.</h3><p>Operations application</p></div></div></section>
<section class="case-section next-questions"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="number">04</span> Continuing the work</div><h2>The next question<br/>is part of the craft.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>The useful next step is to validate how people move through the workflow: whether visitors understand the request status, whether staff can identify the next action, and where branch context needs to be more visible.</p><p>A working system provides the starting point. Observing how it fits into the day informs what to refine next.</p><a href="/blog/designing-for-the-unhappy-path/" class="text-link">Related draft: designing for the unhappy path <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={16}/></a></div></section>
<div class="case-end"><a href="/#work" class="text-link"><Icon name="arrow-left" size={16}/> Back to the portfolio</a><a href="/blog/" class="text-link">Explore the journal <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={16}/></a></div>
</main><Footer/></body></html>
<style>
 .case-intro{padding:45px 0 40px}.back-link{display:inline-flex;gap:12px;align-items:center;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:44px}.back-link:hover{color:var(--accent)}.case-intro .eyebrow{font-size:10px;color:var(--accent)}h1{font-size:clamp(48px,7vw,94px);margin-top:22px}h1>span{color:var(--accent)}.case-subtitle{font:500 38px/1.25 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.04em;color:var(--ink);margin-top:25px}.case-subtitle span{color:var(--muted)}.case-meta{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.4fr 1fr;gap:30px;margin-top:45px;padding-top:25px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.case-meta>div{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px}.case-meta span{font-size:9px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--muted)}.case-meta strong{font-size:12px;font-weight:500}.case-image{margin:0;padding:30px;background:#dbe5df;border-radius:4px;color:#24463e}.image-toolbar{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font:8px var(--font-display);letter-spacing:.1em;margin-bottom:20px}.case-image img{border-radius:4px;box-shadow:0 10px 30px #24463e10;width:100%}.case-image figcaption{font-size:10px;margin-top:20px;color:#486457}.case-section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;gap:90px;padding-block:70px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.case-section h2{font-size:35px;margin-top:23px;line-height:1.2}.case-section .eyebrow{font-size:10px}.case-section .prose{font-size:16px}.evidence-note{font-size:12px;background:var(--surface);padding:16px 20px;border-left:2px solid var(--line)}.decisions{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px}.decisions>div{display:flex;align-items:start;gap:20px}.decisions>div>span{font:10px var(--font-display);color:var(--accent);padding-top:7px}.decisions h3{font-size:23px;margin-bottom:12px}.decisions p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.8}.booking-image{margin-top:65px;background:#e1e5e9;color:#586575}.booking-image figcaption{color:#586575}.stack{display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:25px}.stack .pill{font-size:10px}.flow-section{padding:35px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:60px}.flow-section>.eyebrow{font-size:10px;color:var(--muted)}.flow{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;margin-top:30px}.flow>div>span{font-size:8px;color:var(--accent);letter-spacing:.08em}.flow h3{font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin-block:12px}.flow p{font-size:10px}.flow-arrow{font-size:24px;color:var(--muted)}.next-questions{border-bottom:0}.prose .text-link{font-size:11px;text-decoration:none}.case-end{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:60px;padding-top:20px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.case-end .text-link{font-size:11px}
 @media(max-width:900px){.case-section{gap:40px}.case-section h2{font-size:30px}.case-meta{gap:20px}.flow h3{font-size:20px}.flow{gap:12px}.flow-section{padding:25px}}
 @media(max-width:650px){.case-intro{padding-top:30px}.case-subtitle{font-size:28px}.case-meta{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:20px}.case-image{padding:15px}.image-toolbar{font-size:6px;gap:15px}.case-image figcaption{font-size:9px}.case-section{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:25px;padding-block:45px}.case-section h2{font-size:31px}.flow{flex-direction:column;align-items:start;gap:20px}.flow-arrow{transform:rotate(90deg);margin-left:35px}.flow>div{width:100%;padding:5px 0}.flow h3 br{display:none}.flow h3{font-size:23px}.flow h3 br::after{content:' '}.flow-section{margin-top:35px}.case-end{gap:25px;flex-wrap:wrap}.booking-image{margin-top:40px}}
</style>
